<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX4-QA-008>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX4-QA-008" ;
  triage:title "No mechanical check detects a duplicate Python dict-literal key silently shadowing an earlier entry in .just/lint_boundaries.py IO_FORBIDDEN_SOURCE_PATTERNS" ;
  triage:description "AX.4 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax4-qa-r1, PR #1194 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T09:14Z; found by ruthless-boundary-qa RBQA-F002) at head aaf2e04bf. The 60-plus-key IO_FORBIDDEN_SOURCE_PATTERNS dict literal in .just/lint_boundaries.py has no guard against duplicate keys; the existing test test_every_declared_io_forbidden_tag_has_source_pattern_mapping in .just/tests/test_lint_boundaries.py uses set(dict.keys()) which collapses duplicates, so the AX4-QA-003 shadowing went undetected. Fix: add an AST-based duplicate-key unit test in .just/tests/test_lint_boundaries.py that parses lint_boundaries.py and fails on any repeated key in that dict literal. Note: the test file is not frozen; .just/lint_boundaries.py itself is." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RBQA" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
